  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-05-23T17:16:17.933Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Since recently the VRChat SDK has started to prompt you every so often when you build and upload your avatar for VRChat.\n\nLet me start of by saying I have no problem with agreeing to this, that said, what I do have a problem with is how obtrusive this prompt is.\n\nNot only do you have to keep agreeing to it, the prompt also shows up AFTER building the avatar and right before the upload.- Inconvenient to say the least. Because most creators will be ready with their VR headset on their head after clicking the build button, ready to play with their new creation or test their patches.. Just to realize that, no, your avatar actually isn't uploaded yet because of this prompt.\n\nThis should have never left Q/A as is.\n\n**Here are my suggestions to fix this inconvenience**\n\n- Have a one-time agreement that you click and is saved to your account.\n\n**Or** (if you want to prevent people from claiming ignorance;)\n\n- Have a checkbox that shows up BEFORE you start building your avatars/worlds.\n\nOn a sidenote this agreement is also part of VRChat's TOS so what does it really add?\n\nThanks for your time.\n\n~ Burrely",
